84. THE UX RULE THAT SHOULD GOVERN ALL FUTURE WORK
The user should never think:
“Where do I enter this again?”
They should think:
“I recorded what happened. Verity knows the consequences.”
That's the standard I'd now use to audit every existing Plywood screen.
And this gives us a very clear next implementation pass: stop adding isolated features and connect every existing record through state propagation, Related sections, drill-downs, role-aware actions, and accountant/tax projections.
